    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb3b5dfb_45779528",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2185,
      "author": {
        "id": 1957996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-18T23:52:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At this point if this could be `true` (even without the added code), that would have had broken ChromeOS without SWB support because the codec selection is delegated to Floss, and the audio server will still expect something else.\n\nOne critical flag to block the enablement is probably via hal::get_swb_supported, so that during codec negotiation SWB is completely ignored. I\u0027m not sure if that function is implemented in this patch series (note ChromeOS uses `system/stack/btm/btm_sco_hfp_hal_linux.cc`, which is different from Android\u0027s `system/stack/btm/btm_sco_hfp_hal.cc`).\n\nOtherwise this patch LGTM, but FYI this only affects ChromeOS so it\u0027s OK to hold.",
      "parentUuid": "a965ea1a_854e1f58",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2185,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 2185,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "abb1432f567f11c8211ed78551878add919abdc0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46549f79_2b84384b",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2185,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958755
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-19T10:58:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "in hal interface inside ChromeOS, we return false for `get_swb_supported` in this patch series, so here we would not select LC3 as final codec here `get_hfp_audio_final_codecs` as `SwbCapsUpdate` would not be triggered.",
      "parentUuid": "fb3b5dfb_45779528",
      "range": {
